{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05BE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-constructible-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eb32d009b2922e4f92b9b031d87b65818a960c5a63af0634d1e4ce59b4b8552c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a41bb87904f1e0ab38f53ef3a9690d694124573ad0a2933c3f392a1e2a87f3a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Checking constructibility of a sheaf\nof sets, abelian groups, <MATH_0002>-modules (with <MATH_0003> Noetherian)\ncan be done Zariski locally on <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5f7ba46f16e1a11b77d6cccaec87b8c2787c480724ba2afede4292a417f5a866", "unit_id": "tag:095F:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05BE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$U = \\bigcup U \\cap U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{U \\cap U_i}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}|_U$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-constructible-quasi-compact-quasi-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e1729717e0af7c1fd28b9f8a85efda86fab3ced88368935dcf77c8694b355e4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:713333ffb7f16ad668ec63a2fe81cd0e3ccfd9fd8c762b4f89e71048c22ff775", "source_text": "The statement means if <MATH_0001> is an open covering\nsuch that <MATH_0002> is constructible, then <MATH_0003>\nis constructible. If <MATH_0004> is affine open, then\n<MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> is constructible\n(it is trivial that the restriction of a constructible sheaf to\nan open is constructible). It follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthat <MATH_0007> is constructible, i.e., a suitable partition\nof <MATH_0008> exists.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d52d582b0a69294a14d5fa1322287a4566c7b67461d6d96f74ea5c924d5156f4", "unit_id": "tag:095F:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05BE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$Y_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$X_\\etale$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-constructible}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f6906ea2ca51106b12c9080effac2f0d61c38d254264610292b6fafc1780296a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:07a0b0a5e0ea028699187167f135a5b692795a3f7e08733872072208030dcd6f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes. If <MATH_0002> is a\nconstructible sheaf of sets, abelian groups, or <MATH_0003>-modules\n(with <MATH_0004> Noetherian) on <MATH_0005>, the same\nis true for <MATH_0006> on <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9065b2bfc8d1f13f09cdb10ca0c8db6f4dfa3611dbccaaa35ad995a989ac9bbb", "unit_id": "tag:095G:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05BE", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-constructible-local}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-constructible-quasi-compact-quasi-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-locally-constant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:248ce34c16a2c6d1046c90ed36ab867ff55a86a9610d2c452d1298bba9c2ba71", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d47e5963986056bd39baa0b2856a23b6ff6193220057f9fb05d44a757be7ffc9", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001> this reduces to the case\nwhere <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are affine. By\nLemma <REF_0002>\nit suffices to find a finite partition of <MATH_0003> by constructible\nlocally closed subschemes such that <MATH_0004> is finite locally\nconstant on each of them.\nTo find it we just pull back the partition of <MATH_0005> adapted to\n<MATH_0006> and use\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a5c0b8a4893af57c18b296bcb2a6a4ef5c9c87b72396c6001179ed084db3bab", "unit_id": "tag:095G:proof"}
